   229	
   230	```
   231	branchSolutions = Solve[1 + r^2 - 4*(g - r)^2 == 0, g];
   232	gminus = FullSimplify[Min[g /. branchSolutions], Assumptions -> $Assumptions];
   233	gplus  = FullSimplify[Max[g /. branchSolutions], Assumptions -> $Assumptions];
   234	```
   235	
   236	then add an explicit symbolic-equality check against the closed forms that sympy uses:
   237	
   238	```
   239	expectZero["g_- closed-form match", gminus - (2*rrad - 37*Sqrt[3])/(20*Pi)];
   240	expectZero["g_+ closed-form match", gplus  - (2*rrad + 37*Sqrt[3])/(20*Pi)];
   241	```
   242	
   243	This way the Mathematica script derives `g_±` by symbolic root-finding (independent of the sympy hand-write) and verifies that its derived values match sympy's hand-written closed forms — true cross-engine corroboration on the carry-forward.
   244	
