/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/tmp_prompts/audit_directive_125.md:96:- **(b) Paper is overstating — trim the `Output` claim in the card.** Edit `/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/paper/stages/stage_125.tex:15-17` so that the boxed claim is the *pointwise* kernel bound on `[0,L]` rather than the integral bound on `𝔤[σ]`, and downgrade the notes' two boxes accordingly. This is almost certainly the wrong direction: the notes (lines 33–55) make the integral statement the central deliverable, and the appendix (lines 29 and 86) describes stage 125 as the "positive mouth-source theorem" — which is the integral statement, not the pointwise fact.
